# kernel-sparc-leon3.img -- how it is built, and why it is not just a vmlinux
#
# This image is the only one here that is NOT the raw kernel output.  qemu's
# leon3_generic machine has no PROM and its built-in bootloader only pokes the
# UART and timer registers and jumps to the ELF entry point -- it does not turn
# the MMU on.  sparc32's head_32.S requires both: it reads the romvec from %o0
# and bails out to halt_notsup if the MMU is off.  Loading vmlinux directly
# gives "Trap 0x02 (Illegal Instruction) ... pc: f0004000", because the ELF is
# linked at physical 0xf0000000 while leon3 RAM starts at 0x40000000.
#
# The missing piece is Gaisler's mklinuximg, a GPLv2 second stage loader that
# sets up the MMU tables, builds a romvec and scans the AMBA plug&play bus:
#
#   https://download.gaisler.com/anonftp/linux/linux-6/kernel/mklinuximg-2.0.20.tar.bz2
#
# Build steps (the toolchain is the same one the CI target uses):
#
#   # 1. kernel, from kernel-sparc-leon3.config
#   make -C <linux-6.18.37> O=<obj> ARCH=sparc CROSS_COMPILE=sparc-openadk-linux-uclibc- -j20
#
#   # 2. wrap it.  -cflags is only needed because the toolchain finds no libc
#   #    headers on its own; mklinuximg itself is freestanding.
#   CROSS_COMPILE=sparc-openadk-linux-uclibc- \
#     ./mklinuximg <obj>/vmlinux kernel-sparc-leon3.img \
#       -cmdline "console=ttyS0,38400" -cflags "--sysroot=<sysroot>" -strip
#
# The command line is baked in here, because leon3_generic has no -append.
#
# Rootfs: leon3_generic has no -initrd either, so the rootfs goes into the
# 16M placeholder (kernel-sparc-leon3.cpio, CONFIG_INITRAMFS_SOURCE points at
# "../kernel-sparc-leon3.cpio", CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_NONE=y so the
# signature survives).  Unlike the xtensa/cf5208 placeholders this one takes the
# *xz-compressed* rootfs: unpack_to_rootfs() runs decompress_method() over the
# built-in blob and skips the trailing zeros one byte at a time.  Raw cpio would
# need 80M, because sparc's linker aligns every data segment to 64K and 86% of
# the sparc rootfs is zero padding.
#
# Two version traps:
#
#   Kernel.  drivers/tty/serial/apbuart.c is broken between v6.3 and v6.7:
#   apbuart_tx_chars() asks uart_port_tx_limited() for "port->fifosize >> 1"
#   characters, and qemu's APBUART model reports no FIFO depth, so
#   apbuart_scan_fifo_size() returns 1 and the count is 0 -- nothing is ever
#   transmitted.  printk still works (it polls), so the kernel log looks
#   perfect while userspace output vanishes.  Before v6.3 the loop was a
#   do/while that always sent one character; v6.8 dropped the ">> 1".  Stay
#   outside that window or carry a one-line patch.
#
#   qemu.  Every qemu from 9.0.0 on fails to boot leon3_generic with -kernel,
#   Gaisler's own reference image included: it exits silently after ~50ms with
#   no output.  Bisected to 92688a91c358, which dropped the stack pointer from
#   the machine's reset handler without putting it into the synthetic
#   bootloader; see qemu-leon3-bootloader-sp.patch next to this file, which is
#   what the qemu-system-sparc in qemu-inst.tar.xz carries.  A distribution
#   qemu does not have that patch, so this target cannot be run with
#   "uc_devel -q --system-qemu" until the fix is upstream.
#
#   This image is uniprocessor.  An SMP kernel needs qemu-leon3-smp.patch as
#   well (also in qemu-inst.tar.xz): without it the IRQMP reports no broadcast
#   and the second CPU dies on its first swapa.
